{
  "$comment": [
    "Kody's animations, the single source: tools/kodygen.py turns each entry into kody/kody_<name>.c and",
    "declares them all in include/kui_kody_anims.h. The Lottie files beside this one are copied unchanged",
    "from kody-ui (AnimacionesKody/03-lottie); the poses that draw them live there.",
    "An entry reframes its source onto a canvas of w x h: every top-level layer is scaled by 'scale' about",
    "the origin and moved by (dx, dy), so a point (x, y) of the source lands on (scale x + dx, scale y + dy).",
    "Canvases sit on the glass's bottom edge, all but cargando's, a 264 x 264 square centred on the glass",
    "(the wheel's 342 px brought down to 260, 2 px clear of each side). The face's animations share one",
    "410 x 300 canvas (screen y 202 to 502): the clock family is lifted out of its full-glass source by",
    "202 px, and the train, rooftop, camping, small-hours and mallet families, drawn for a 410 x 288 canvas",
    "214 px down, are let down 12 px into it.",
    "'anchor' is the number of frames between two anchor poses, 0 for an animation that has none; it divides",
    "the pass. The rooftop, camping, small-hours and mallet loops have none: each tells one story a pass, and no",
    "period brings frame 0's picture back. 'recolour' replaces a colour exactly, compared at 8 bits per",
    "channel, alpha kept: the train's wall, and the glass of the small-hours window with the disc that cuts",
    "its moon, are drawn in the design's page colour, and the Dot's page is true black.",
    "An entry with 'builtin' is also compiled into the firmware: the reloj scene, the floor a board falls",
    "back on when no pack is usable. 'pack' is the official pack, in the firmware's format (kui_pack.h) but",
    "naming entries: kodygen writes each entry as pack/<name>.json.z and this block as pack/kode.json, with",
    "every digest, and takes each scene's anchor from its loop's entry."
  ],
